{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"At present I still feel yesterday in my bones, for it was a day of hard marching. — After the writing lesson I had with you — I mean, without having first called on you, I could not go out — I went first once more to the Princely Liechtenstein Gallery; — if I were to go there ten more times, I would not exhaust its treasures; — stood in it until 12 o'clock, — then to Währing, — that gallery is nearly half an hour away, — from there, — to visit my colleague, the Professor of the local Chair of Philosophy, Rembold — not as old as I am, a proper fellow countryman of mine, to whom my writings are not unknown), — only the people here] all stay too much cooped up, — traveling and getting about does not come so easily to them as to us. — From there I crossed a branch of the Danube and went to the Augarten for lunch, — never so tasty and so cheap as in my inn, where the fatal carriage meal takes place, and ate with a good appetite; afterwards I looked around in the Augarten. The garden is maintained just like the one in Schönbrunn, — broad, grand avenues, — the trees, shrubs in the paths cut into vertical flat walls, the trees like fans, or as if you left the stem on a pear and cut it into a disc on it, about as thick as the stem is, — so that one walks only between trees, not under trees and foliage, and always has the sky, which today was indeed so beautifully blue, above one's head; also the sun is already lower, so there is shade from the walls. — But at the end of the Augarten there is a view of the richest countryside, which has the hills about an hour away — Leopoldsberg, Kahlenberg — as its boundary, — in the most beautiful light the most beautiful landscape! — For such spots we are to be envied here. — Afterwards to the Prater — a forest, as I love it, with green grass, without any undergrowth and bushes between the tree trunks; — besides an innumerable number of taverns, bowling greens, carousels, optical room travels etc., I found some very elegant coffee pavilions here one writes correctly Kaffeh) — finally, after long wandering about, out of fatigue, to rest, to the Leopoldstadt Theatre, where Schuster played a Magister quite excellently, otherwise spoke High German; the second was again the Magic Pear, and went, very tired, in the most beautiful moonlight, — the fine weather is unchangeably faithful — home and to supper"}}],"created":1795219070,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":558,"prompt_tokens":720,"total_tokens":1278,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-BLIj8dMFythqyre3Wt4cJRbQ83ErC1BO","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":720,"prompt_ms":773.988,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0749833333333334,"prompt_per_second":930.2469805733421,"predicted_n":558,"predicted_ms":13126.341,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.56614183123878,"predicted_per_second":42.433759720244964}}